# WP-BP-010 StageGraph

- Read the canonical StageGraph specification, `WP-BP-010-stagegraph-runtime.md`,
  `IMPLEMENTATION_READINESS.md`, accepted dependency evidence, and
  `PARALLEL_WORKTREE_PROTOCOL.md` before editing.
- Own only StageGraph regions in shared control-plane/compiler/orchestration modules.
- Keep run control, generic operation execution, Deep Agents materialization, async delegation,
  root workflow, and registries read-only unless the integrator approves an explicit amendment.
- Replace the batch `asyncio.gather()` frontier with deterministic incremental child
  reconciliation. Interpreter proposals never become lifecycle authority.
- Move accepted mechanics into `app/temporal/workflows/stagegraph.py`; delete the legacy flat
  workflow, direct-activity family path, and Agent Server macro graph at acceptance.
- Add deterministic join/property/fairness/invalidation/obligation tests, Temporal replay/recovery,
  and a credential-gated live API-to-Temporal test using real LLM calls. The live graph must prove
  downstream release before an unrelated slow sibling finishes.
- Use a minimal exact Deep Agent binding; defer the complete advanced-capability vertical to
  `WP-CP-050`.
